.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd November 14, 2026
.Dt NQB2B 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqb2b
.Nd BLAKE2b, keyed and unkeyed
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Ft int
.Fo nqb2b
.Fa "const uint8_t *key" "size_t keylen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *in" "size_t inlen"
.Fa "uint8_t *out" "size_t outlen"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn nqb2b
writes the BLAKE2b digest of the
.Fa inlen
bytes at
.Fa in
to
.Fa out ,
.Fa outlen
bytes long (1 to 64; the length is part of the hash, so a 32-byte digest
is not the start of a 64-byte one).
With
.Fa keylen
from 1 to 64 it is the keyed hash of RFC 7693, a MAC: compare tags with
.Xr nqcteq 3 ,
never
.Xr memcmp 3 .
With
.Fa keylen
0,
.Fa key
may be
.Dv NULL .
.Pp
The time taken depends only on the lengths, never on the key or the
data.
There is no incremental interface; the library's Argon2id
.Pq Xr nqa2id 3
uses BLAKE2b inside.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Dv NQOK ,
or
.Bl -tag -width NQEARG
.It Bq Er NQEARG
.Fa outlen
is 0 or over 64,
.Fa keylen
is over 64,
.Fa out
is
.Dv NULL ,
or
.Fa key
or
.Fa in
is
.Dv NULL
with a nonzero length.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
uint8_t d[64];
int rc = nqb2b(NULL, 0, (const uint8_t *)"abc", 3, d, sizeof d);
/* d is BLAKE2b-512("abc"), ba 80 a5 3f ... */
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 3 ,
.Xr nqa2id 3 ,
.Xr nqcteq 3 ,
.Xr nqhash 3
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC 7693.
The tests check appendix A, the self-test of appendix E, and keyed and
unkeyed answers of every message length 0 to 255 and every output
length.
